course: dictionary
lesson: 8099
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word remover has two main meanings. The first is a substance that takes something off, such as nail varnish remover. The second is a person or company that moves your furniture to a new house, used mostly in the UK.
explain: «Sand does not dissolve in water, because its particles are joined too strongly for water to pull them apart; nail varnish does not dissolve in water either, but it does dissolve in nail varnish remover.» Dissolve means to mix into a liquid so that it disappears. Here, the nail varnish disappears into the remover, so remover must be the substance meaning.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. If the sentence is about a stain, paint or varnish, it is the substance. If it is about a sofa being carried into a new home, it is the company or the people. Try your meaning in the sentence, just as you would with any new word.
fact: A remover is a substance used to take something off, such as nail varnish remover, stain remover or paint remover.
fact: In the UK, removers can also be people or a company that moves your furniture to a new house. This is a removal company.
fact: Remover is a noun, and it has a plural: removers.
fact: «Dissolve» means to mix into a liquid so that it disappears.
fact: Removers are chemicals, so keep them away from small children and use them with fresh air.
exercise: What is a stain remover used for? | To paint a wall bright colours | To keep food cold | *To take a stain off something | To mend a torn sleeve
exercise: In «nail varnish does dissolve in nail varnish remover», what does the remover do to the varnish? | It makes the varnish harder to remove | It adds a new colour to the nails | *It dissolves it so it can be wiped away | It makes the varnish shine brighter
exercise: Why must removers be kept away from small children? | *They are chemicals that can harm small children | They are only sold in shops for adults to read about | They taste sweet, so children eat them | They are too heavy for children to lift
test: A removal company will move your furniture to your new house. Which meaning of remover is this? | *A person or company that moves furniture | A chemical that takes off paint | A brush for painting walls | A tool for cutting wood
test: Why should you use nail varnish remover with fresh air? | Because it needs sunlight to work | Because fresh air makes it work better in the cold | Because fresh air makes it smell nicer | *Because it is a chemical, and fresh air keeps you safe
exam: Which sentence uses remover to mean a company? | *The removers carried the sofa up the stairs into our new house | The nail varnish remover is on the bathroom shelf | The stain remover lifted the mud off my jumper | The paint remover must be kept away from children
